lesson: 234
title: Points in a game
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: In basketball a basket scored from inside the line is worth 2 points, a three-pointer 3 points and a free throw 1 point.
explain: Multiply each kind of score by its points, then add the three amounts.
explain: 4 baskets, 2 three-pointers and 3 free throws: 4 × 2 + 2 × 3 + 3 × 1 = 8 + 6 + 3 = 17 points.
vars: a=name b=2..12 t=2..6 f=2..8 k=2..9
answer: b * 2 + t * 3 + f
exercise: In a basketball game, {a} scores {b} baskets, {t} three-pointers and {f} free throws. How many points does {a.he} score?
exercise: A basketball team scores {b} baskets, {t} three-pointers and {f} free throws in the first half. How many points is that?
exercise: How many points does {a} get for {t} three-pointers, {b} baskets and {f} free throws?
exercise: {a} made {f} free throws, {b} baskets and {t} three-pointers in the final. How many points did {a.he} score?
exercise: In one quarter, the Tigers score {b} baskets from close in, {t} three-pointers and {f} free throws. How many points do they score in the quarter?
exercise: {a} got {b} baskets, {t} threes n {f} free throws. points?
exercise: ok so {b} baskets, {t} three pointers, {f+1} free throws — no wait {f}. how many points
